<title>USA: US CPI overstatement has big budget impact - panel.</title>
<headline>US CPI overstatement has big budget impact - panel.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1996-12-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Consumer Price Index (CPI) substantially overstates the cost of living and that has &quot;dramatic ramifications&quot; for the federal budget, the head of a commission that studied the subject said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>Stanford University Professor Michael Boskin, who led the congressionally-appointed commission, said that much of the overstatement can be fixed but that it will take a while.</p>
<p>&quot;We are all going to need some time,&quot; he told reporters.</p>
</text>
